#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186381041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124465 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8702032e-0795-5b51-9cc9-f89b35b64fa0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain Where a Partial Derivative Exists"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c364cfd-1479-5837-b69d-fc5890b52b72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381043} {:answer/id #uuid "623d5eb7-6cf1-5331-839b-8940d4542054" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z\\ne 0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,x+y\\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381044} {:answer/id #uuid "777163a6-4575-5fe2-bab5-3a222ca8472d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,x+y\\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381045} {:answer/id #uuid "cf30651e-fd1f-5379-8ed6-0cbbd9c71c7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y\\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381046} {:answer/id #uuid "32457ba4-7abb-5686-9625-22909bdbfa3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,x+y>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "777163a6-4575-5fe2-bab5-3a222ca8472d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,x+y\\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381045} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b9accac-db82-5666-ad16-3e0dc26f02fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186381042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0b90b4c-4db3-51f6-8299-2c96c4e8e47d" :question/math-academy-id "q-132639" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)}{x+y},$ find the set of values $(x,y,z)$ on which $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}$ exists." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)$ is defined only when \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & >0\\,\\text{and}\\,x+y\\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,x+y\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivative of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z)}{x+y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+y}\\cdot \\frac{1}{z} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{z(x+y)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function ${f}_{z}(x,y,z)$ is defined only for \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z(x+y) & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of ${f}_{z}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{z}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z\\ne 0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,x+y\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $z$ exists on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,x+y\\ne 0}\\cap {(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z\\ne 0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,x+y\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,z>0\\,\\,\\text{and}\\,\\,x+y\\ne 0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124465 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8702032e-0795-5b51-9cc9-f89b35b64fa0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain Where a Partial Derivative Exists"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3daceeb4-5e80-5f8f-85bd-515962379d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}\\ge 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321630} {:answer/id #uuid "428e3bac-c800-558d-bac2-a851af87d4b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}<0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321673} {:answer/id #uuid "be3b2462-0f26-5fb6-a489-2d8bcd809916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322623} {:answer/id #uuid "cce381d1-8d0e-56d7-8fdd-9d65cbeacc24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}\\le 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322742} {:answer/id #uuid "e2950ea4-bbca-5065-aeba-1ee54fee9a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${f}_{x}$ exists everywhere on the $xy$-plane" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322917}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be3b2462-0f26-5fb6-a489-2d8bcd809916" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322623} :answer-field/id #uuid "5763486d-1d53-542c-85cd-250f90996edf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9763ffd8-3c44-5d6e-88c3-a58aee03c56a" :question/math-academy-id "q-36624" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}+{y}^{2}),$ find the set of values $(x,y)$ on which $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ exists." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y)$ is defined only when \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+{y}^{2} & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}>0}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivative of $f(x,y)$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}+{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ is defined only for \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+{y}^{2} & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $x$ exists on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}} & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}>0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{3}+{y}^{2}>0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124557 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2d7d4db-e9e1-54a0-aadb-42447771855d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain Where All Partial Derivatives Exist"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28861c2c-ac02-5058-a869-4e0465790ba2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,y>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333364} {:answer/id #uuid "667aa589-f213-58d8-80cb-0bd6003e45d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy\\ge 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333924} {:answer/id #uuid "b2322b57-77ca-5063-9b19-1f81d4ecf5f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334552} {:answer/id #uuid "b6f16518-f4d1-5447-8c6d-28607b0b21e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy<0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334591} {:answer/id #uuid "d8b23563-bef9-5ca0-84f5-e8348fe229b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2322b57-77ca-5063-9b19-1f81d4ecf5f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334552} :answer-field/id #uuid "4339d5d0-363f-5656-970d-cbfe0eaaac6f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0790aa49-4020-5e37-b9fd-2a18a4aa638d" :question/math-academy-id "q-65252" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)$ and\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy),\\,\\frac{∂f}{∂y}=\\frac{x}{y},\n$$\n\nfind the set of values $(x,y)$ where all partial derivatives of $f$ exist." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)$ is defined only when $xy>0.$ So, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0}.\n$$\n\nAs for the partial derivatives, we have the following.\n\n- The function ${f}_{x}(x,y)=1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(xy)$ is defined only when $xy>0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{x}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{x}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0}.\n$$\n\n- The function ${f}_{y}(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}$ is defined only when $y\\ne 0.$ So, the domain of ${f}_{y}$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{y}}={(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partials of $f$ exist on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{x}}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{y}} & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0}\\cap {(x,y)\\,:\\,y\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,xy>0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339041 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124465 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8702032e-0795-5b51-9cc9-f89b35b64fa0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain Where a Partial Derivative Exists"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "120d95db-561e-5ca1-ac7c-781d4f73d592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z\\ge 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336201} {:answer/id #uuid "57e0038e-1359-539c-a31a-4273eee9f3f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z=0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336837} {:answer/id #uuid "bf81d1cd-2f00-5c28-8b65-d9f0805741aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z\\le 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337733} {:answer/id #uuid "eeedecdd-29bc-53af-b9a1-39073c0ad4c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z\\ne 0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338122} {:answer/id #uuid "f21d2a1a-323a-5715-849a-37c24d5f3e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338151}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f21d2a1a-323a-5715-849a-37c24d5f3e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338151} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd98808-554a-5bf7-a091-d7cf355fddd2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aa160777-02b6-5c38-ab2e-1a2020472567" :question/math-academy-id "q-72000" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+z),$ find the set of values $(x,y,z)$ on which $\\frac{∂f}{∂z}$ exists." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $f(x,y,z)$ is defined only when \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z & >0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of $f$ is \n\n$$\n{D}_{f}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivative of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y+z)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+y+z}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function ${f}_{z}(x,y,z)$ is defined only for \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+z & \\ne 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the domain of ${f}_{z}$ is\n\n$$\n{D}_{{f}_{z}}={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z\\ne 0}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that the partial derivative of $f$ with respect to $z$ exists on the set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{f}\\cap {D}_{{f}_{z}} & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0}\\cap {(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z\\ne 0} \\\\  & ={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,x+y+z>0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
